            <title>[LU-7056] sanity test_27c: FAIL: 1 != 8</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7056</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Bob Glossman &amp;lt;bob.glossman@intel.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.hpdd.intel.com/test_sets/51e7d43c-4d40-11e5-862f-5254006e85c2" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.hpdd.intel.com/test_sets/51e7d43c-4d40-11e5-862f-5254006e85c2&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sub-test test_27c failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;1 != 8
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this looks a bit like old bug &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-3712" title="sanity 27c: 0 != 7" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-3712"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-3712&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, but that was fixed a long time ago.&lt;br/&gt;
maloo search shows a fair number of similar looking FAILs with no specific bug attached, so I'm raising a new one.  It may be a dup of some other known bug I can't identify.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Info required for matching: sanity 27c&lt;/p&gt;</description>
